name c01m01-slaughterzone
timeout 900
time 1994-10-07T06:00:00Z

# ARMORED FIST (NovaLogic 1994), CAMPAIGN ONE "OVERWATCH", MISSION 1 OF 7 — `INDIA1`, SLAUGHTERZONE!
# Spec, provenance and every open question: mods/armored-fist/doc/campaign.md,
# mods/armored-fist/doc/terrain.md, mods/armored-fist/doc/substitutions.md. Format: doc/missions/syntax.md.
#
# THE TASK [FSW]: find and neutralise the Indian FORWARD BASE, including all patrolling MBT/IFV and
# ALL ARTILLERY EMPLACEMENTS. Course 036 NNE. Time limit 15 min [FSG, SHDR byte 5].
#
# ---- THE SEVEN DISCLOSURES THAT APPLY TO ALL SEVEN FILES. Stated in full HERE; the other six carry
# ---- the short form and point back at this file. Full table: doc/substitutions.md.
#
# D1  THIS IS A TANK GAME AND THERE IS NO TRACKED VEHICLE IN THIS TREE. Nothing drives, nothing on the
#     ground perceives, nothing on the ground shoots: `sensors/FBRadarSystem` and `FBIrstSystem` skip
#     every unit that is not `FBUnitKind::Aircraft`, `FBVisualSystem` keeps only units whose catalogue
#     DECLARES an extent and both ground classes declare 0, and `modules/ground/FBGroundModule::Run` is
#     empty by design. NO VEHICLE MODEL WAS INVENTED (CLAUDE.md Prinzip 1). Echo company's M1A2 and M3
#     therefore fly as `module f16`, ONE JET PER VEHICLE of the [GUIDE] order of battle, and the
#     direction of that error is not a nuance: an F-16 with a canister levels in one pass what a tank
#     platoon needs an afternoon and its own losses for. Every goal that falls here falls to the wrong
#     weapon delivered by the wrong vehicle. What is preserved is the mission's SHAPE — its axis of
#     advance, its objective list, its order of battle and its clock.
#
# D2  RED CANNOT SHOOT BACK, ANYWHERE IN THIS CAMPAIGN. A T-80, a BMP-2, a bunker and an artillery
#     emplacement are all `target_soft`/`target_hard`: a pose, an extent and a fragility, with no
#     sensor, no weapon and no motion. No source read for Overwatch names a SAM or an AAA position
#     (campaign.md §3.1 lists bunkers, artillery, dishes, tanks, mines and Hinds — no air defence), so
#     declaring one to give blue an opponent would be invention. CONSEQUENCE, STATED ONCE: `objective
#     survive` is unfalsifiable in all seven missions, the loss half of every reading rule below can
#     never fire, and no mission in this campaign is LOSABLE. That is the campaign's headline finding.
#
# D3  ONE PASS PER UNIT, WHICH IS WHAT SETS EVERY MISSION'S ARITHMETIC. `pilot/FBPilot::AttackCommands`
#     latches `AtkReleased_` after the single pickle, turns out and returns to the route phase; nothing
#     resets it. So a delivery unit delivers exactly ONE weapon at exactly ONE aim point, a mission with
#     11 flagged goals needs 11 aim points, and the number of aim points a mission can service is the
#     size of Echo company. THE DELIVERY DOCTRINE, applied identically to all seven files:
#       (a) aim points are the [FSW] task's own named elements first, then the [GUIDE] Bandit platoons
#           in table order, minus any platoon the mission's reading rule forbids engaging;
#       (b) surplus delivery units repeat the BANDIT list from the top carrying `mk84` aimed at that
#           platoon's first T-80 — the second pass exists to reach what the canister cannot;
#       (c) the weapon is the aim point's class: `cbu87` on any cluster holding a `target_soft`,
#           `mk84` on a pure `target_hard` cluster.
#
# D4  THE TWO FRAGILITY CLASSES ARE THE WHOLE LADDER, and the campaign's outcome is decided by them.
#     `modules/ground/FBGroundTarget.h` has exactly two rungs. T-80 and every bunker -> `target_hard`
#     (Mk 84 fail radius 17.7 m, CBU-87 flux 8 % of threshold = NOTHING). BMP-2 and every installation
#     -> `target_soft` (Mk 84 fail radius 100 m, CBU-87 kills anywhere in its 400 x 200 m footprint).
#     A 14-tonne IFV is not a house: `target_soft` overstates its fragility, in blue's favour. An MBT
#     under a 2000 lb bomb dies well beyond 17.7 m: `target_hard` understates it, against blue.
#     THE PREDICTION THIS MAKES, before any run: canisters kill the soft half of a platoon and every
#     installation; T-80s and bunkers survive unless a Mk 84 lands inside 17.7 m.
#     THE PREDICTION HELD — 29 deliveries across the seven files, mean `aimErrM` 46.0 m (18.4 … 71.9),
#     ZERO inside 17.7 m, and not one `target_hard` destroyed anywhere in the campaign.
#
# D4a THE RUN-IN LENGTH IS THIS CAMPAIGN'S DECISIVE [SET] NUMBER, and it was measured AFTER the fact
#     rather than tuned before it. Every file flies 40 km. Isolated on the f16 fixture's own flat
#     geometry — same store, same 900 m AGL, same 450 kt, ONE variable:
#       25 km run-in (`mods/f16/src/missions/attack-ccrp.fbm`)  aimErrM 12.41  across +10.99
#       40 km run-in, heading 090                               aimErrM 40.04  across -33.93
#       40 km run-in, heading 000                               aimErrM 42.61  across -36.87
#     The error is a function of the LEG'S LENGTH, not of the heading and not of these coordinates: the
#     attack leg is anchored where the pass begins (`pilot/FBPilot::AttackCommands`) and the lateral
#     hold OVERSHOOTS on a long one — the sign flips between 25 and 40 km, so it oscillates rather than
#     drifts. CONSEQUENCE, STATED PLAINLY: at 25 km a Mk 84 would land inside `target_hard`'s 17.7 m
#     fail radius and T-80s would begin to die, so THIS CAMPAIGN'S RED RESULT IS PARTLY THE CHOICE OF
#     40 km. 40 km stays, because it was chosen for the approach march before any of this was measured
#     and shortening it now would be tuning the scenario until it passes. The lever is named and
#     numbered instead.
#
# D5  THE GROUND IS REAL AND THE ORIGINAL'S IS NOT. `src/data/sindh-dem-90m.bin` is Terrarium z13 baked
#     onto a 90 m grid over 24.65-27.10 N / 66.55-71.40 E (5402 x 3017, min -33 m, max 2028 m, mean
#     144.0 m, 0 holes, /elev agreement bias +0.14 m rms 1.63 m over 400 points), so `--elev baked` is
#     the default and every altitude here is ASL over the real Thar and lower Indus. The original loads
#     GREEN, WET voxel maps for six of these seven missions while its own campaign map draws the Thar
#     desert (terrain.md §5); faithfulness to the original and to the real place pull apart, and this
#     tree takes the real place. Ground under the seven objectives: 21-249 m.
#
# D6  THE ANCHORING IS A RECONSTRUCTION FROM A PRINTED MAP. Every centre is terrain.md §3-4: a
#     plate-carree fit to three cities on [GUIDE p.53], worst residual 9 km, Barmer surviving as a
#     probe it never saw. Everything within a mission is laid out from that centre by the run-in
#     bearing, which is the [FSW] course. WHAT IS NOT DERIVABLE: the game's world unit -> metre scale
#     is UNDETERMINED (terrain.md §6, three attempts, all failed), so no distance INSIDE a battlefield
#     comes from the original. The 2 km platoon separations and the 40 m vehicle spacing below are
#     [SET], and 40 m was chosen for a reason that is itself a measurement: a 4-vehicle platoon then
#     spans 120 m of frontage, and against the CBU-87's 100 m half-width plus this tree's ~25 m
#     across-track delivery error every vehicle stays under the footprint — so the outcome is decided
#     by the WEAPON and not by the author's seating plan. Measured on the way here: at 55 m spacing
#     (165 m frontage) the outboard vehicle fell outside and survived. The classes are INTERLEAVED
#     (T-80, BMP, T-80, BMP) for the same reason — all-BMPs-outboard would have made the footprint edge
#     pick the survivors. A real platoon at 100 m spacing would lose its flankers, and the world scale
#     that would settle which is right is UNDETERMINED. Named, not hidden.
#
# D7  THE CLOCK'S DATE IS [SET] AND ITS HOUR IS A READING OF THE DATA. No source gives a story date;
#     1994-10-07 is the retail CD's own file date, the only date any source in this tree carries. Local
#     -> UTC is -5 h [DERIV, Pakistan Standard Time, the theatre's western half and the army the player
#     advises]. Day missions run 1100 PKT = 0600Z. ONLY `INDIA5` loads `7.SKY` [FSG] — one fifth the
#     size of every other sky and absent from the editor's map table, i.e. the night sky — so only
#     mission 5 is flown at night, and the guide's claim that mission 2 is the first night mission is
#     contradicted by mission 2's own daylight sky/palette pair (campaign.md §4b).
#
# ---- WHAT THIS FILE DECLARES
#   Blue [GUIDE p.54]: Echo 1 = 1 M1A2 + 1 M3. Two vehicles, two jets, two passes.
#   Red  [GUIDE p.54]: Bandit 1 (2 T-80, 2 BMP), Bandit 2 (2 T-80, 2 BMP), Bandit 3 (2 T-80).
#     [GUIDE p.55] calls this 5-to-1 against; 10 red vehicles against 2 blue is 5-to-1 exactly, which is
#     the one place a guide number and a guide table check each other in this campaign.
#   The FORWARD BASE and the ARTILLERY EMPLACEMENTS are named in the [FSW] task and are the mission's
#   goals. NEITHER CARRIES A COUNT in any source, and the goal flag that would settle it lives in the
#   undecoded `DCBS` chunk (campaign.md §7.4), so each is declared ONCE. The direction is understated.
#
# READING RULE (binding). The verdict is `m1e1a`'s UNIT_RESULT and nothing else.
#   The [FSW] task is "the forward base INCLUDING all patrolling MBT/IFV and all artillery
#   emplacements", so SUCCESS/exit 0 requires ALL TWELVE declared red objects dead inside 900 s.
#   TIMEOUT/exit 3 with a named subset dead is the EXPECTED result and is NOT an engine defect: two
#   passes cannot service four aim points (D3) and no weapon here reaches a T-80 (D4). Read the
#   `mission UNIT_RESULT` lines, count DESTROYED against INTACT, and report the split.
#   exit 1 on `m1e1a` is an ENGINE finding, not a mission loss: nothing in this file can shoot at it
#   (D2), so a blue FAIL means the airframe departed controlled flight or CFIT'd on its own.
#   exit 2 = a unit died that nobody declared. Engine finding either way.

unit m1e1a
  module f16
  team friendly
  flight echo1 1
  spawn 26.41501 69.73087 980 36.0 450        # 40 km short of the base on the [FSW] course 036
  set gear up
  set fuel_int_pct 100
  set fcr_mode off                            # a striker does not radiate, and there is nothing to see
  set rwr on
  set store 3 cbu87
  set brief_master_arm arm
  set task attack
  set attack_mode ccrp
  wp 26.70660 69.96730 980 450                # AIM POINT: the forward base, 900 m over its own 75.1 m
  wp 26.88884 70.11507 1580 450               # egress 25 km up the axis
  objective kill unit m1base
  objective kill unit m1arty
  objective kill unit m1b1v1
  objective kill unit m1b1v2
  objective kill unit m1b1v3
  objective kill unit m1b1v4
  objective kill unit m1b2v1
  objective kill unit m1b2v2
  objective kill unit m1b2v3
  objective kill unit m1b2v4
  objective kill unit m1b3v1
  objective kill unit m1b3v2
  objective survive

unit m1e1b
  module f16
  team friendly
  flight echo1 2
  spawn 26.40707 69.74304 990 36.0 450        # 1.5 km across track from the M1A2's substitute
  set gear up
  set fuel_int_pct 100
  set fcr_mode off
  set rwr on
  set store 3 cbu87
  set brief_master_arm arm
  set task attack
  set attack_mode ccrp
  wp 26.72458 69.96590 990 450                # AIM POINT: Bandit 1, the nearest patrolling platoon
  wp 26.88884 70.11507 1590 450
  objective survive

# ---- THE OBJECTIVE AREA. Installations on the axis of advance, 150 m apart, so one canister covers
# ---- both; the [FSW] task names them and gives no count (D6).
unit m1base
  module target_soft
  team hostile
  spawn 26.70660 69.96730 ground 36.0 0
unit m1arty
  module target_soft
  team hostile
  spawn 26.70769 69.96819 ground 36.0 0       # 150 m up-axis of the base

# ---- BANDIT 1 [GUIDE p.54]: 2 T-80, 2 BMP. Four vehicles across the axis at 40 m = 120 m of frontage,
# ---- interleaved, inside the CBU-87's 100 m half-width by construction (D6).
unit m1b1v1
  module target_hard
  team hostile
  spawn 26.72490 69.96541 ground 36.0 0
unit m1b1v2
  module target_soft
  team hostile
  spawn 26.72468 69.96573 ground 36.0 0
unit m1b1v3
  module target_hard
  team hostile
  spawn 26.72447 69.96606 ground 36.0 0
unit m1b1v4
  module target_soft
  team hostile
  spawn 26.72426 69.96639 ground 36.0 0

# ---- BANDIT 2 [GUIDE p.54]: 2 T-80, 2 BMP. No delivery unit left for it (D3).
unit m1b2v1
  module target_hard
  team hostile
  spawn 26.72150 69.97863 ground 36.0 0
unit m1b2v2
  module target_soft
  team hostile
  spawn 26.72129 69.97896 ground 36.0 0
unit m1b2v3
  module target_hard
  team hostile
  spawn 26.72107 69.97928 ground 36.0 0
unit m1b2v4
  module target_soft
  team hostile
  spawn 26.72086 69.97961 ground 36.0 0

# ---- BANDIT 3 [GUIDE p.54]: 2 T-80, no IFV.
unit m1b3v1
  module target_hard
  team hostile
  spawn 26.71107 69.98665 ground 36.0 0
unit m1b3v2
  module target_hard
  team hostile
  spawn 26.71085 69.98698 ground 36.0 0
